# Implementation Plan: Complete Separation of Girls PG & Boys PG Systems

The objective is to establish a completely segregated system for **Girls PG** and **Boys PG**, ensuring strict privacy, distinct enrollment pipelines, customized building rules, and allowing PG owners to independently manage both Boys and Girls branches under one account.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> ### 1. Strict Gender-Based Access & Isolation
> - **Student Experience**:
>   - Students specify their gender during signup (`Female` / `Male`).
>   - **Automatic Filtering**: A female student only sees and can enroll into **Girls PGs** (or Co-Ed); a male student only sees **Boys PGs**.
>   - **Backend Security Check**: A student cannot use a Girls PG join code if their profile is Male, and vice versa.
> - **PG Type Classification**:
>   - Every PG property is tagged with `pgType`: `'girls' | 'boys' | 'co-ed'`.
>   - Visual badges everywhere: `🌸 Girls PG` vs `🔷 Boys PG`.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> ### 2. Owner Multi-Branch Switcher (1 Owner, Multiple PGs)
> - If an owner operates both a **Boys PG** and a **Girls PG**:
>   - They don't need two different email accounts.
>   - A sleek **Branch Switcher** dropdown in the Navbar lets the owner toggle between e.g. `🏢 Shanti Boys PG` and `🌸 Shanti Girls PG`.
>   - Each branch has its own independent **Rooms**, **Residents**, **Complaints**, **Notices**, **Join Passcode**, and **Rules**.

